const LABEL: Record<State, { text: string; cls: string }> = {
  checked: { text: "checked", cls: "done" },
  model: { text: "model only", cls: "accent" },
  open: { text: "open", cls: "gap" },
};
const count = (rows: Claim[], s: State) => rows.filter((r) => r.state === s).length;
const ALL = [...CONSENSUS, ...JOURNAL];
---
<Doc title="Engineering" kicker="Engineering" section="engineering/" siblings={[]}
  description="The safety case of paros-consensus and of the journal: each claim, the TLA+ model that states it, the trace check and the walk that hold the code to it, and the mutants that must die. The open rows stay on the page.">

  <div class="strip" aria-label="The safety case in figures">
    <div><span class="k">Claims</span><span class="v">{ALL.length}</span></div>
    <div><span class="k">Checked on the code</span><span class="v">{count(ALL, "checked")}</span></div>
    <div><span class="k">Model only</span><span class="v">{count(ALL, "model")}</span></div>
    <div><span class="k">Open</span><span class="v">{count(ALL, "open")}</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="read">How to read it</h2>
  <p>Each row is one safety claim. A claim is <b>checked</b> when three judges hold the code that
  ships to it: TLC checks a <a href={url("engineering/tla/")}>TLA+ model</a> that states the
  claim as an invariant; a seeded <a href={url("engineering/simulation/")}>walk</a> runs the real
  state machines with faults on, and an oracle with no code of its own judges it; TLC checks the
  trace of each walk against the model. A claim is <b>model only</b> when its model is checked
  and its code is not built yet. A claim is <b>open</b> when something is not proved; its issue
  says what.</p>
  <p>Each judge is tested too. A control is a TLC check that must fail without the rule. A <a href={url("engineering/mutants/")}>mutant</a> is a bug planted in the driver of a walk,
  and its oracle or its trace check must fail.</p>
  <div class="callout">
    <p><b>Mostly bounded.</b> TLC explores small instances of each model completely. Only the
    single decree has a proof that holds at every size (TLAPS); the other claims do not have
    one yet: that is the last row of the first table (<a href={ISSUE(1307)}>#1307</a>).</p>
  </div>

  {[
    { id: "consensus", title: "paros-consensus", rows: CONSENSUS, intro: "The sans-IO Paxos roles. Every walk runs the real ColocatedNode, ProxyLeader, ReplicaNode and Matchmaker of the crate." },
    { id: "journal", title: "The journal", rows: JOURNAL, intro: "The journal v1. Its pure core (paros-journal: the fold, Resolve and the matchmaker register) has walks; its roles, controller and driver are not built yet, so most rows are model only." },
  ].map((g) => (
    <>
      <h2 id={g.id}>{g.title}</h2>
      <p>{g.intro}</p>
      <table class="case">
        <thead><tr><th>Claim</th><th>Model · invariant</th><th>Trace spec</th><th>Walk · oracle</th><th>Must die</th><th>State</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {g.rows.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <td data-label="Claim">{r.claim}{r.note && <span class="case-note">{r.note}</span>}</td>
              <td data-label="Model"><div>{r.models.length ? r.models.map((m) => (
                <span class="case-item"><a href={`${TLA}/${m.dir}`}><code>{m.dir}/</code></a>{m.inv.length > 0 && <> {m.inv.map((i) => <code>{i}</code>).reduce((a: any, b: any) => [a, ", ", b])}</>}</span>
              )) : <span class="case-none">none</span>}</div></td>
              <td data-label="Trace"><div>{r.trace.length ? r.trace.map((t) => (
                <span class="case-item"><a href={`${BLOB}/${t}`}><code>{t}</code></a></span>
              )) : <span class="case-none">none yet</span>}</div></td>
              <td data-label="Walk"><div>{r.walk ? r.walk : <span class="case-none">none yet</span>}</div></td>
              <td data-label="Must die"><div>
                {r.controls.length > 0 && <span class="case-item">TLC: {r.controls.map((c) => <code>{c}</code>).reduce((a: any, b: any) => [a, ", ", b])}</span>}
                {r.mutants.length > 0 && <span class="case-item">walk: {r.mutants.map((m) => <code>{m}</code>).reduce((a: any, b: any) => [a, ", ", b])}</span>}
                {r.controls.length + r.mutants.length === 0 && <span class="case-none">none</span>}
              </div></td>
              <td data-label="State"><div><span class={`chip-status ${LABEL[r.state].cls}`}>{LABEL[r.state].text}</span>{r.issue && <span class="case-item"><a href={ISSUE(r.issue.n)}>#{r.issue.n}</a> ({r.issue.name})</span>}</div></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </>
  ))}

  <h2 id="sources">Where each row comes from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The models and their checks: <a href={`${TLA}`}><code>specs/tla/</code></a>, with <code>checks.txt</code> in each folder. A name under <i>TLC</i> is a check of that file
      whose listed result is <code>violation</code>.</li>
    <li>The walks, oracles and mutants of the core: <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/crates/sim/consensus-sim`}><code>consensus-sim</code></a> (<code>Flavor</code> and <code>Mutant</code> in <code>src/cluster/flavor.rs</code>, the oracles in <code>src/oracle/</code>).
      A walk name is a <code>Flavor</code>.</li>
    <li>The walks of the journal: <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/crates/sim/journal-sim`}><code>journal-sim</code></a> (<code>src/fold.rs</code>, <code>src/register.rs</code>).</li>
    <li>The rule behind each journal row, with its decision: <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/journal/07-verification.md`}>§J7.1</a> of <code>docs/journal/</code>. The flavor view of the core: <a href={url("consensus/proof/")}>How it is checked</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="pages">The techniques</h2>
  <ol class="index-list">
    <li><a href={url("engineering/tla/")}>TLA+ models</a><span class="desc">No code before its model. TLC checks each rule, each rule has a control, and each guard of a model is mutated.</span></li>
    <li><a href={url("engineering/simulation/")}>Simulation</a><span class="desc">Seeded walks with faults on the code that ships, each walk checked against its model, every probe reached. No exception.</span></li>
    <li><a href={url("engineering/mutants/")}>Mutants and assertions</a><span class="desc">cargo-mutants on the core, the score of a dated run, and the hard assertions that stop a broken state.</span></li>
    <li><a href={url("engineering/grid-quorums/")}>Grid quorums</a><span class="desc">Partitions of acceptors: a write touches one, an election touches all. Stop acceptors and see what still works.</span></li>
  </ol>
  <p>The sans-IO core and its driver loop are in <a href={url("consensus/driver/")}>Consensus</a>.</p>
</Doc>
